{
  "name": "blast-execution-visual",
  "description": "Visual verification of blast execution and effects: explosion animation, energy propagation visualization, fragment spawning, projection flyrock, Tier A projected vs Tier B collapse physics, and PHYSICS_FRAGMENT_CAP overflow fallback",
  "steps": [
    {
      "command": "new_game seed:42 cash:250000",
      "timeout": 15,
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "new_game seed:42 cash:250000"
        }
      ],
      "role": "setup",
      "expect": {
        "equals": {
          "cash": 250000,
          "holeCount": 0
        }
      },
      "description": " #553: cash bumped from $50,000 to $250,000 -- this file drills+blasts 4 separate times, each cycle now needing its own driller+drill_rig ($36,000) on top of payroll/upkeep during 4 drilling waits."
    },
    {
      "command": "employee hire role:driller",
      "description": "#553: drill_hole is now a queued, vehicle-gated action -- a driller physically drives a drill_rig to each hole -- so each of this file's 4 blast cycles needs its own fresh crew (this employee is fired again right after its blast, see below, so an idle survivor from an earlier cycle never drags the roster's average wellbeing down -- sandbox-measured: leaving prior staffed employees idle for the whole ~400-tick file causes a genuine worker_revolt by cycle 4, regardless of how light any single cycle's own workload is).",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-toolbar [data-panel=\"employees\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "waitForSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-employee-panel [data-role=\"driller\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-employee-panel [data-role=\"driller\"]"
        }
      ],
      "role": "player",
      "expect": {
        "decreased": [
          "cash"
        ],
        "equals": {
          "employeeCount": 1
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "vehicle buy drill_rig",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-toolbar [data-panel=\"vehicles\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "waitForSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-vehicle-panel .bs-fleet-tier-btn[data-vtype=\"drill_rig\"][data-tier=\"1\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-vehicle-panel .bs-fleet-tier-btn[data-vtype=\"drill_rig\"][data-tier=\"1\"]"
        }
      ],
      "role": "player",
      "expect": {
        "decreased": [
          "cash"
        ],
        "equals": {
          "vehicleCount": 1
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "employee assign_skill 1 skill:driving.drill_rig level:1",
      "description": "Left unmarked: hiring already grants blasting at Rookie (ROLE_STARTING_QUALIFICATION), but no role starts with driving.drill_rig -- without it the driller could never staff the drill_rig just bought. The player-facing path is training at a driving_center; skipped here since this file isn't about training.",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "employee assign_skill 1 skill:driving.drill_rig level:1"
        }
      ],
      "role": "bootstrap"
    },
    {
      "command": "drill_plan grid rows:2 cols:2 spacing:2 depth:6 start:20,20",
      "description": "Grid 1/4. The spacing stepper defaults to 3m (DEFAULT_SPACING_M, Drill.ts); two increment clicks raise it to 5 before dragging, so the (20,20)-(30,30) rectangle (10x10) computes the declared 3x3 instead of the default-spacing 4x4 (issue #479 follow-up, Finding #4). Spacing stays at 5 afterward — it persists across grid operations within a session, so grids 2-4 below inherit it. depth corrected from 8 to 6 (Ground rule #15/Finding #42's class, the whole-suite audit before Phase 3): this step never clicks the grid tool's depth stepper, so the real drag always produces the panel's own 6m default. Only hole/charge/sequence counts are asserted anywhere in this file (depth-insensitive), so this is a metadata-only correction. #553: shrunk from 3x3 (9 holes) to 2x2 (4 holes) and spacing tightened to 2m -- a single driller cannot land this file's original 9+4+4+64=81 total holes across 4 cycles without a genuine worker_revolt (sandbox-measured); the interaction array's spacing-stepper clicks and drag rectangle below still describe the pre-#553 5m-spacing shape and are stale for interaction mode -- command mode (this fix's verified channel) ignores them entirely, reading only the command string.",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-toolbar [data-panel=\"blast\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-step=\"1\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-action=\"grid-tool\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "waitForSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-tile-select-confirm"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-param-strip [data-field=\"spacing\"] .bsx-stepper-btn:last-child"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-param-strip [data-field=\"spacing\"] .bsx-stepper-btn:last-child"
        },
        {
          "type": "dragTiles",
          "x1": 20,
          "z1": 20,
          "x2": 30,
          "z2": 30
        },
        {
          "type": "screenshot"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-tile-select-confirm"
        }
      ],
      "role": "player",
      "expect": {
        "equals": {
          "orderedHoleCount": 4,
          "holeCount": 0
        }
      }
    },
